# References and links: a marker inside another pair of braces, {{page}}, is written as text.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: References and links · Writing a marker as text
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Section:
		Text: References and links
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Writing a marker as text
		Paragraph: A marker inside another pair of braces is written as text and is not replaced: `{{{page}}}` writes `{{page}}`, the marker itself. It works for every marker and in any text. Other texts between braces are not markers and are written as they are.
			Style: intro
		Text: Text: This is page {{page}} of {{pages}}.
			Style: label
		Text: This is page {page} of {pages}.
			Style: target
		Text: Text: The footer is written {{{page}}} of {{{pages}}}.
			Style: label
		Text: The footer is written {{page}} of {{pages}}.
			Style: target
		Text: Text: Dear {{name}}, see {{{page of: terms}}}.
			Style: label
		Text: Dear {{name}}, see {{page of: terms}}.
			Style: target
